  "findings": [
    "Retriever is semantic guideline-chunk search wrapper, not file/image duplicate detector. Blank query returns[]; any backend exception logs debug and returns[] indistinguishable from no matches. has_index delegates count without catch. Source-only, no vectorstore/model invoked.",
    "Two init markers verified empty. Prior screening evidence is not automatically credited as full-source review. No code adopted.",
    "Fingerprint means language/framework/profile classification by extensions/markers, not content hash or duplicate detection. _walk uses rglob then filters ignored-parent paths after traversal, so ignore list is not directory-pruning work bound; no file/depth/cancel/completeness report. Source-only, no user directory scanned.",
    "Nested package.json triggers has_package_json but framework detection reads root/package.json only; nested-only framework dependencies can be missed. has_pyproject flag assigned but unused. Invalid manifest JSON shape can escape handling because only OSError/JSONDecodeError caught.",
    "Generic PLC XML sampling affects language counts but summarize primary percentage derives only extension mapping, omitting generic XML confirmations; PLC primary can display0percent. XML sample selection depends traversal order and first5000total file cutoff; not deterministic full vendor coverage. No code adopted.",
    "Offline original-function controls with replacement data holder confirm nested React package marker detected but frameworks empty, and sole Siemens-signature generic XML classified plc_siemens while summary reports0percent. Pydantic/full suite not executed; temporary files only.",
    "C++ tool resolves requested target and rejects outside-root paths before runner invocation; missing runner/path and runner exceptions become textual errors. Actual subprocess timeout/resource behavior delegated to unread runner/context. No analyzer executed.",
    "All returned findings appended to pending_findings while display caps50; display limit is not scan/result storage work bound. Repeated tool invocation can append same finding again here, with downstream consolidation not yet reviewed. No file/image duplicate engine and no code adoption.",
    {
      "path": "src/revio/layers/static/cppcheck.py",
      "scope": "whole pinned file, static inspection; analyzer not executed",
      "observations": [
        "subprocess timeout defaults to 300 seconds; capture_output buffers stdout and stderr with no output byte cap in this wrapper.",
        "Return code is not checked when XML exists; any parseable XML without error nodes yields an empty result, with no validation of results root/version or explicit completeness status.",
        "XML is accepted only when stripped stderr or stdout begins with the XML declaration; progress before the declaration is not extracted despite the comment about interleaved progress.",
        "scan_to_findings drops diagnostics without primary locations and missingIncludeSystem.",
        "Resolved paths outside repo_root are retained as original file paths when relative_to raises ValueError; caller target validation does not validate each emitted diagnostic path."
      ],
      "transfer_to_dedup": "Keep scan completion and tool failure distinct from zero matches; bound buffered subprocess output. No implementation copied."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/revio/agent/findings_store.py",
      "observations": [
        "Identity is truncated SHA1 over path, line and normalized title, not file content equality.",
        "Repeated fingerprints in the same record_run increment run_count per finding rather than per run.",
        "Updates replace finding_json but leave severity/category/confidence/title columns unchanged; isolated control confirms stale severity.",
        "Missing/unreadable current source line falls through to still_present; deleted source file confirmed by control.",
        "Default history retention is unbounded; list_all materializes all rows; compare opens a connection per finding."
      ],
      "controls": "docs/research/dedup-500/revio242-findings-store-controls-20261025.json",
      "original_tests_run": false
    },
    {
      "path": "src/revio/layers/rag/indexer.py",
      "observations": [
        "Embedding singleton is shared across all requested model names; vectorstore cache keyed only by persist directory.",
        "index_documents forwards each call with no stable IDs, source replacement or duplicate check in this wrapper; fake backend confirms repeated additions forwarded. Actual Chroma duplicate semantics not executed.",
        "count and list_sources collapse backend errors to empty values; clear suppresses delete errors and evicts cached object.",
